  "notes": "Uplifting and vocal trance's central figure, with a dance-pop crossover wing; the band spans the entry's three documented ranges (132-142 uplifting, 120-135 house-leaning, 126-130 pop crossover) and is centred at 134. Three trance conventions the research states verbatim do the work. \"Minor keys almost universal\" is a 7:2 minor weighting and no major scale at all. \"Kick on every downbeat, de-emphasised relative to the bassline\" plus \"the low end is a texture, not a punctuation\" gives the quietest accent tier among the producer models here against a continuous rolling 16th bass at 0.96 roots — the low end never stops. And \"lengthy snare rolls building in velocity, frequency and volume toward the end of a measure as the primary transition device\" is an authored ramp with a near-zero gap and descend probability and the ladder on. The arrangement is the canonical form the entry spells out: a mid-song climax \"followed by a soft breakdown that disposes of beats and percussion entirely, leaving melody and atmospherics alone for an extended stretch\" — a 32-bar bridge and the highest drop-out probability in this section. Loops are 8 or 16 bars. ⚠ The act-specific tempo detail is convention-derived by the entry's own statement, and every velocity, density and register above is INFERRED.",
